{"availability":"available","full":"NinoMdev/Plantnet2Anki","name":"Plantnet2Anki","description":"A tool allowing atomated creation of Anki decks from your Plantnet observations.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-10T08:00:08Z","updated":"2026-08-13T20:57:03Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://plantnet2anki.onrender.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.810Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.810Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.810Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:38:02.047Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:41.314Z","stars":4,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.810Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project automates the creation of an Anki deck (.apkg) from your personal observations in PlantNet. Anki's built-in import option \"Update existing notes when first field matches\" allows you to incrementally update your deck with new observations without resetting its learning state. Anki is a highly efficient tool for memorising things like botany, so I believe this project could be very useful for any botanist who wants to retain their field observations more effectively. This is initially a personal project that I am sharing because I think it can be useful to others.","Enjoy, and don't hesitate to share any comments or suggestions. I am not a developer, so some features may be missing and bugs may occur.","This project was coded with the assistance of Claude AI."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NinoMdev/Plantnet2Anki/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f00fceb11a82d3352de95dadb48c9867ba1e796539dff27b989dcbaedc6fe2d1","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:52.124Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:19:09.494Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-13T20:57:03Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project automa